        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4d059560-9517-506c-9374-79d0b5f03ac6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- TV Episodes: Empty Orchestra\n- TV Series: Inside No. 9, Paradox, EastEnders, Red Cap, New Tricks\n- People: Steve Pemberton, Reece Shearsmith, Guillem Morales, Tamzin Outhwaite, Sarah Hadland, Emily Howlett, Javone Prince\n- Roles: Melanie Owen, Detective Inspector Rebecca Flint\n- Broadcasters: BBC One, BBC 2\n\nFacts:\n- From 1998 to 2002, Tamzin Outhwaite played Melanie Owen in the BBC One soap opera EastEnders and came to national notice through that role.\n- After EastEnders, Tamzin Outhwaite starred in theatre and television productions including Red Cap and New Tricks.\n- In 2009, the British science fiction police drama Paradox starred Tamzin Outhwaite as Detective Inspector Rebecca Flint.\n- Empty Orchestra is the fourth episode of the third series of the British dark comedy anthology television programme Inside No. 9.\n- Empty Orchestra was written by Steve Pemberton and Reece Shearsmith, directed by Guillem Morales, and first aired on BBC 2 on 7 March 2017.\n- Empty Orchestra is set in a karaoke booth and follows work colleagues Greg, Fran, Connie, Janet, and Duane as they celebrate the promotion of Roger.\n- In Empty Orchestra, Greg is played by Reece Shearsmith, Fran by Sarah Hadland, Connie by Tamzin Outhwaite, Janet by Emily Howlett, Duane by Javone Prince, and Roger by Steve Pemberton.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "93a25772-2015-5100-b8a5-2b77d04aa069",
        "text": "Page: Empty Orchestra. Sentence: \"Empty Orchestra\" is the fourth episode of the third series of the British dark comedy anthology television programme \"Inside No. 9\".\nPage: Empty Orchestra. Sentence: Written by Steve Pemberton and Reece Shearsmith and directed by Guillem Morales, the episode first aired on 7 March 2017, on BBC 2.\nPage: Empty Orchestra. Sentence: The episode is set in a karaoke booth, and follows a group of work colleagues—Greg (Shearsmith), Fran (Sarah Hadland), Connie (Tamzin Outhwaite), Janet (Emily Howlett) and Duane (Javone Prince)—celebrating the promotion of Roger (Pemberton).\nPage: Tamzin Outhwaite. Sentence: Since coming to national notice playing Melanie Owen in the BBC One soap opera \"EastEnders\" from 1998 until 2002, she has since starred in both theatre and television productions, including army series \"Red Cap\" and crime drama \"New Tricks\".\nPage: Paradox (TV series). Sentence: Paradox is a 2009 British science fiction police drama, starring Tamzin Outhwaite as Detective Inspector Rebecca Flint.",
